    <name>
      <text>Direct Variation 4 - Graph (interactive)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The cost, \(C\), of maize (in hundreds of Ksh) varies directly as its mass, \(m\), in kg: \(C = km\). The graph shows this relationship, and \(P\) is a point on the line.</p>
[[jsxgraph input-ref-ans2="ans2Ref" width="500px" height="450px"]]
var board = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[-1,38,9,-3], axis:true, grid:true, showCopyright:false, showNavigation:false});
var line = board.create('line', [[0,0],[1,{#pk#}]], {strokeColor:'blue', fixed:true});
var P = board.create('point', [{#pr#},{#pk*pr#}], {name:'P', fixed:true, color:'red', size:4});
var A = board.create('point', [1,1], {name:'A', snapToGrid:true, snapSizeX:1, snapSizeY:1, size:5});
stack_jxg.bind_point(ans2Ref, A);
[[/jsxgraph]]
<p>(a) Use the point \(P\) to find the constant \(k\).</p>
<p>\(k = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>(b) Drag the point \(A\) to the point on the line where \(m = {@px2@}\) kg. The coordinates of \(A\) appear in the box below.</p>
<p>\(A = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>The point \(P\) is \(({@pr@}, {@pk*pr@})\), so \(k = \frac{C}{m} = \frac{ {@pk*pr@} }{ {@pr@} } = {@pk@}\).</p>
<p>The line is \(C = {@pk@}m\). When \(m = {@px2@}\): \(C = {@pk@}({@px2@}) = {@pk*px2@}\), so \(A = ({@px2@}, {@pk*px2@})\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
